      "math_academy_id": "q-60139",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio",
      "problem": "One day, $20$ adults and some children attended a music festival at Beethoven Park. If the ratio of adults to children was $4:7$, how many people attended the park that day?",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $4:7$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of adults and the denominator represents the number of children.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $20$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\times 5}{7\\times 5}=\\frac{20}{35}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20$ adults and $35$ children attended that day. Thus, the total number of people who went to the park that day was\n\n$$\n20+35=55.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
