      "knowledge_point": "Calculating an Amount Given a Ratio as a Fraction",
      "problem": "A bag contains blue and green buttons. The ratio of blue buttons to the total number of buttons is $2:7.$ If there are $14$ blue buttons,  how many green buttons are in the bag?",
      "worked_solution": "We are given that the ratio of blue buttons to the total number of buttons is $\\frac{2}{7}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of blue buttons, and the denominator represents the total number of buttons.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $14$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 7}{7\\times 7}=\\frac{14}{49}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are a total of $49$ buttons in the bag. \nSo, the number of green buttons is\n\n$$\n49-14=35.\n$$",
